Quick tips and next steps:
- Why acrylic: fast-drying, versatile, easy cleanup, and great for beginners.
- Starter supplies: acrylic paint set (student or artist grade), synthetic brushes (flats and rounds, sizes 6–12), pre-primed stretched canvas or canvas board, gesso (if priming), palette (plastic/paper), palette knife, water jar, paper towels, and an acrylic medium (retarder or gloss/matte medium) and final varnish.
- Good beginner brands: Liquitex Basics, Winsor & Newton Galeria, or Arteza (student grade); Golden for higher-end.
- Short workflow: prime (if needed) → block in large shapes → build layers, working from dark to light → add details → varnish when fully dry.

